{"notices":[{"id":"USN-8958-1","title":".NET vulnerabilities","summary":"Several security issues were fixed in .NET","instructions":"In general, a standard system update will make all the necessary changes.","references":[],"published":"2026-10-29T17:02:55.501527","description":"It was discovered that the .NET Blazor WebAssembly debug proxy did not\nproperly escape certain values. An attacker could possibly use this issue\nto execute arbitrary code. The fix for this CVE was originally released via\nUSN-8942-1, but it was found to be incomplete. This issue only affected\ndotnet10 and dotnet11. (CVE-2026-102870)\n\nIt was discovered that the Brotli decompression library used by .NET\nincorrectly handled certain compressed streams. A remote attacker could\npossibly use this issue to cause a denial of service or execute arbitrary\ncode. (CVE-2026-111497)\n\nAlen Cheung discovered that .NET did not properly handle file ownership in\ncertain circumstances. An attacker could possibly use this issue to elevate\nlocal privileges. (CVE-2026-114148)","is_hidden":false,"release_packages":{"jammy":[{"name":"dotnet8","version":"8.0.133-8.0.33-0ubuntu1~22.04.1","description":".NET CLI tools and runtime","is_source":true},{"name":"aspnetcore-runtime-8.0","version":"8.0.33-0ubuntu1~22.04.1","is_source":false,"is_visible":true,"source_link":"https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/dotnet8","version_link":"https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/dotnet8/8.0.133-8.0.33-0ubuntu1~22.04.1","pocket":"security"},{"name":"aspnetcore-runtime-dbg-8.0","version":"8.0.33-0ubuntu1~22.04.1","is_source":false,"is_visible":false,"source_link":"https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/dotnet8","version_link":"https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/dotnet8/8.0.133-8.0.33-0ubuntu1~22.04.1","pocket":"security"},{"name":"aspnetcore-targeting-pack-8.0","version":"8.0.33-0ubuntu1~22.04.1","is_source":false,"is_visible":false,"source_link":"https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/dotnet8","version_link":"https://launchpad